So I think the next question that I will select, did the migration process help you identify GXP gaps and close them?

00:55:45.609 --> 00:55:46.609
I can talk about it.

00:55:46.609 --> 00:55:49.609
I was just responding to that question, actually.

00:55:50.609 --> 00:55:54.609
So we have done – basically, it's a major shift.

00:55:54.609 --> 00:55:58.609
We have historically been using SAS Grid.

00:55:58.609 --> 00:56:05.609
And we are basically migrating out, and there are multiple questions from a data perspective as well as platform perspective.

00:56:05.609 --> 00:56:11.609
So I think the key strategy is to separate the platform from the migration effort.

00:56:11.609 --> 00:56:13.609
So we did the platform first, qualified it.

00:56:13.609 --> 00:56:21.609
So as you can remember, the timeline, we started this in September 2024, and the platform was live in December 2025, SAS Viya.

00:56:21.609 --> 00:56:27.609
And we were basically talking about the specific inventory of what has to be migrated.

00:56:27.609 --> 00:56:30.609
We are not talking about some 10 gigs, 10, 20 gigs.

00:56:30.609 --> 00:56:32.609
We are talking about 150 terabytes.

00:56:32.609 --> 00:56:39.609
And the key aspect is we don't want any regulatory issues because that's being actively used for submissions and responses.

00:56:39.609 --> 00:56:42.609
So that's basically through our entire migration strategy.

00:56:42.609 --> 00:56:47.609
We had multiple try-runs to essentially ensure that we got what we needed, and there were some nuances.

00:56:47.609 --> 00:56:48.609
It was not easy.

00:56:48.609 --> 00:56:53.609
So the old platform was LATIN1, and the new platform, SAS Viya, by default was UTF-8.

00:56:53.609 --> 00:57:00.609
So we have to basically have a compatibility mode to ensure that both the UTF-8 as well as LATIN1 have to be enabled.

00:57:00.609 --> 00:57:03.609
So it has to be tested, but you have to give sufficient time.

00:57:03.609 --> 00:57:05.609
You should not rush through the migration, especially.

00:57:05.609 --> 00:57:07.609
Thanks.

