00:57:50.609 --> 00:57:58.609
So can POSIT become the enterprise SC across clinical development, biostat submissions, and RWE?

00:57:58.609 --> 00:58:00.609
Just to summarize this question.

00:58:00.609 --> 00:58:01.609
Yeah.

00:58:01.609 --> 00:58:04.609
Okay.

00:58:04.609 --> 00:58:18.609
So I think that any one platform has the ability to become the platform to go around and fulfill all of these different use cases.

00:58:18.609 --> 00:58:22.609
And POSIT has many great features.

00:58:22.609 --> 00:58:27.609
It has AI embedded in ways that some of the competition is not at this moment.

00:58:28.609 --> 00:58:37.609
And it's coming up with various ways of observability and also utilizing trusted codes and so on and so forth, like the commons, for example.

00:58:37.609 --> 00:58:43.609
I feel that the question is ultimately going to sort of go back to…

00:58:44.162 --> 00:59:00.162
I feel that the question is ultimately going to sort of go back to the developers, their talent base, how they're used to doing things, and the way that they can sort of migrate and move towards a new sort of an environment.

00:59:00.162 --> 00:59:29.162
And given that we are at the pace at which software is developing, the pace at which new analytical platforms and systems and so on is coming about, I feel strongly, and this is personal views, I feel strongly that the real answer here is to go for a best-in-breed hybrid environment with principles and values as a focus and tools and platforms as the means by which you accomplish those principles.

00:59:29.162 --> 00:59:51.162
Because tools might come and go, but values and principles should stay. And if we follow that approach, I think what we're seeing is today we have the best-in-breed with us, right? We have SAS, we have Posit, we have Databricks, and each one of them can individually become its own only platform for a client or a sponsor or a CRO and so on and so forth.

00:59:51.162 --> 01:00:08.162
But what we're finding is that bringing these things together, having them play in an environment with common shared values and principles, we're getting something that is more than just the sum of its parts. And that's been greatly beneficial to our users.

01:00:08.162 --> 01:00:19.162
That's a great answer. So with that, we'll end our webinar today. Thanks everyone for joining, and we look forward to seeing you on our next webinar.

